dsh has no stable release: every tag is an alpha or a release candidate, and
this is the version npm's latest dist-tag names. Its README: "DeepSeek
Harness is in _developer preview_ and iterating rapidly. THERE WILL BE
COMPATIBILITY-BREAKING CHANGES."

dsh is one npm package for every platform. manifest.json records its tarball:
the SHA-256 of the bytes the registry serves, and the registry's own sha512
integrity. The tarball is the CLI; its 86 dependencies are not pinned here.
No package is bundled and this pin alone does not install or run dsh.
